(4773986, 687659, 90793, '<td valign="top">Hello Everyone<br/> <br/>I wish to thank everyone for voting in my first entry :D I''m really thrilled to start in the top ten and hopefully would remain there ;)<br/> <br/>A special thanks to my Model <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=54033" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">HighNooner</a>, to whom his expressions were highly rated by many people! (probably a bit overrated :P)<br/> <br/>As for the Photo it''s a classic Acid Base reaction, where by chance i saw a documentary, they claimed that the juice of red Cabbage is infact an Acid/Base indicator , where i n neutral solution its remains dark purple(two cups) and in Acid solution it''s Red, while in a Base solution it''s Blue. it was very fun to set up , despite the funky cabbage smell lol.<br/> <br/>The controvertial hour glass was just an ornament on that shelf and landed in the picture, i think it had a nice symbollic effect adding some character to the picture !<br/> <br/>Ahmad<br/></td>', 'Hello Everyone I wish to thank everyone for voting in my first entry :D I''m really thrilled to start in the top ten and hopefully would remain there ;) A special thanks to my Model  HighNooner, to whom his expressions were highly rated by many people! (probably a bit overrated :P) As for the Photo it''s a classic Acid Base reaction, where by chance i saw a documentary, they claimed that the juice of red Cabbage is infact an Acid/Base indicator , where i n neutral solution its remains dark purple(two cups) and in Acid solution it''s Red, while in a Base solution it''s Blue. it was very fun to set up , despite the funky cabbage smell lol. The controvertial hour glass was just an ornament on that shelf and landed in the picture, i think it had a nice symbollic effect adding some character to the picture ! Ahmad', '2008-06-18 04:30:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4773992, 687567, 52549, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hotpasta:</b></div><hr/><i> ....I am speechless...<br/> <br/>Is there no end to your talent?????<br/> <br/>No, I think I know what you are up to...you take <b>PERFORMANCE ENHANCING PHOTOGRAPHY DRUGS </b>and this is the syringe! You have been caught! I will report this to the site council immediately...get your urine sample ready Irene, they''ll be at your door momentarily... </i></td></tr></table> <br/>LOL!! Enzo, I''ll send you my urine sample per post and you can pass it on to the site council ;-D</td>', 'Originally posted by hotpasta: ....I am speechless... Is there no end to your talent????? No, I think I know what you are up to...you take PERFORMANCE ENHANCING PHOTOGRAPHY DRUGS and this is the syringe! You have been caught! I will report this to the site council immediately...get your urine sample ready Irene, they''ll be at your door momentarily...  LOL!! Enzo, I''ll send you my urine sample per post and you can pass it on to the site council ;-D', '2008-06-18 04:33:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4774037, 687567, 41337, '<td valign="top">Congrats Irene! Now why are you surprised? Haven''t you won 50 ribbons this year??? You should be surprised when you don''t win.</td>', 'Congrats Irene! Now why are you surprised? Haven''t you won 50 ribbons this year??? You should be surprised when you don''t win.', '2008-06-18 05:35:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4774040, 687491, 30982, '<td valign="top">I didn''t recognize you (then again, I didn''t vote, either) but I would have recognized the angle of the test tubes perhaps.  Very well done and congrats on another ribbon!  You and Irene and Hotpasta need to keep this up to keep our dear Timfy in his place.  :-)</td>', 'I didn''t recognize you (then again, I didn''t vote, either) but I would have recognized the angle of the test tubes perhaps.  Very well done and congrats on another ribbon!  You and Irene and Hotpasta need to keep this up to keep our dear Timfy in his place.  :-)', '2008-06-18 05:38:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4774051, 687213, 93636, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments.<br/> <br/>As it was shot at ISO 100 I suspect what people identified as noise was actually an artefact of my applying USM badly -- next time I''ll note the settings so people can put me right! In retrospect I should have used bounce flash or lit the scene more, though, as a there were a couple of more interesting shots that suffered some motion blur.<br/> <br/>The background was a worry to me when I was taking the shot, but I couldn''t do much about it. The aperture was already wide open, though I guess if I''d moved in a bit there might have been an extra stop at the wide end of the zoom. Anyone have any tips for blurring the background with a Lumix DMC-FZ50? I''ve struggled to manage it so far :(<br/> <br/>Still, 4.1 -&gt; 4.8 is a definite improvement...</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments. As it was shot at ISO 100 I suspect what people identified as noise was actually an artefact of my applying USM badly -- next time I''ll note the settings so people can put me right! In retrospect I should have used bounce flash or lit the scene more, though, as a there were a couple of more interesting shots that suffered some motion blur. The background was a worry to me when I was taking the shot, but I couldn''t do much about it. The aperture was already wide open, though I guess if I''d moved in a bit there might have been an extra stop at the wide end of the zoom. Anyone have any tips for blurring the background with a Lumix DMC-FZ50? I''ve struggled to manage it so far :( Still, 4.1 -> 4.8 is a definite improvement...', '2008-06-18 05:52:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4774080, 687567, 18450, '<td valign="top">Fantastic shot Irene!!! Congratulations (((hugs)))</td>', 'Fantastic shot Irene!!! Congratulations (((hugs)))', '2008-06-18 06:51:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4774138, 687567, 86836, '<td valign="top">Thanks for explaining how this was done.  I see photos like this all the time and am like "How did they do that?"  I am going to practice and try something like this for fun.  Thanks for explaining and great shot</td>', 'Thanks for explaining how this was done.  I see photos like this all the time and am like "How did they do that?"  I am going to practice and try something like this for fun.  Thanks for explaining and great shot', '2008-06-18 07:56:03.000000', NULL, 0),
